  "external_assumptions": {
    "bootstrap": "Hosted runner provides Python with tarfile.data_filter, HTTPS CA roots and an existing POSIX shell; Windows requires an explicit Git Bash executable with cygpath. No rustup download or installation is used.",
    "macos": "Runner macos-15/macOS-26 supplies the selected Xcode SDKs, clang, linker, codesign and notarization tools. Their runner image and installed Xcode version are recorded; Xcode is not installed or changed here. XcodeGen and CMake archives are verified here (Mac app/CLI CMake4.4.3; iOS CMake4.4.4).",
    "android": "Ubuntu 24.04 supplies C/C++ tools. Android JDK, SDK, NDK and cargo-ndk have separate fixed archive pins in scripts/android-release-inputs.json; Gradle uses its checksum-pinned wrapper and reviewed dependency metadata. CMake, DBus headers and pkg-config use the fixed noble APT snapshot.",
    "windows": "windows-2025 supplies Visual Studio/MSVC, Windows SDK, LLVM clang and Git Bash. windows-build-local.ps1 validates the installed MSVC environment; this helper installs verified .NET10.0.402, NSIS3.13, CMake4.4.4 and NASM3.02 archives without Chocolatey. No Visual Studio or SDK installer is fetched.",
    "linux": "Host Rust here covers Ubuntu24.04 Rust gates and Android host tools. Linux desktop uses separately pinned Ubuntu26.04 distro Rust; Linux CLI uses its separately pinned Debian/Rust container. This installer does not replace either container compiler."
  },
